## T6 · Key comparisons

::: table | Comparisons examiners like in Topic 6.
@widths 3.4,5.3,5.3
@font 9.5
Aspect | One side | The other side
Government vs governance | Institutions holding state power | The whole process of managing public affairs, incl. markets and civil society
Suffragists vs suffragettes | Peaceful, lawful (NUWSS 1897, Fawcett) | Militant direct action (WSPU 1903, Pankhurst)
Descriptive vs substantive representation | Representatives resemble the people | Representatives act for their interests
Critical mass vs critical actors | About 30% women changes institutions (Dahlerup) | Committed individuals drive change (Childs and Krook)
Reserved seats vs candidate quotas | Guarantee a result (Pakistan's 60) | Guarantee an opportunity (5% tickets)
General-seat vs reserved-seat women | Elected in constituencies; funds and base | Party-list; no constituency; party-dependent
Glass ceiling vs glass cliff | Invisible barrier to the top | Appointed to lead in a crisis, when failure is likely
Incremental vs fast track | Slow growth over decades (Nordic) | Quotas jump to critical mass at once
:::
